.TH WERKMEISTER-DAEMON 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-daemon \- The host daemon (the MCP server on port 3002)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister daemon\fR [command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The host daemon is the werkmeister MCP server on port 3002 (\fBoverrides.mcp_port\fR). The VS Code extension, the SessionEnd stop and the scheduler reach it over HTTP. On macOS, launchd keeps it up once it is installed; elsewhere \fBwerkmeister infra connect\fR starts it with a PID file.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBstatus\fR says whether it is serving, which build it loaded (\fBstale (loaded <x>, on disk <y>)\fR after a rebuild or upgrade), and whether the launchd agent is installed and current.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBinstall\fR writes or refreshes the launchd agent: the same step \fBwerkmeister machine setup\fR offers.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBuninstall\fR removes the agent and stops launchd's copy; \fBinfra connect\fR starts it again.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBrestart\fR restarts it, through launchd when launchd owns it.
.PP
Under launchd the daemon restarts itself on a new build: once its entry changes and no call or queued feature is in flight, it exits and launchd starts it on the new code. A PID\-file daemon only reports \fBstale\fR; run \fBrestart\fR. The CLI warns once per run when it reaches a daemon on another build.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister daemon status
werkmeister daemon install
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
